So the bug is: TBEGIN was incorrectly decoded with 2 operands (a register and an unknown), but the printer expected it to have a u1imm operand at position 1. When the decoder decoded TBEGIN, it created a register operand (CRRC0) at position 0 and an unknown operand at position 1. But the printer called `printU1ImmOperand(MI, 1, O)` which reads the imm value of operand 1. Since operand 1 was an unknown type (not an immediate), its `ImmVal` field was uninitialized.

